gmr|n|A tuft, or other excrescence or natural ornament, growing on an animal's head; the comb of a cock; the swelling on the head of a serpent; the lengthened feathers of the crown or nape of bird, etc. ; The plume of feathers, or other decoration, worn on a helmet; the distinctive ornament of a helmet, indicating the rank of the wearer; hence, also, the helmet. ; A bearing worn, not upon the shield, but usually above it, or separately as an ornament for plate, liveries, and the like. It is a relic of the ancient cognizance. See Cognizance, 4. ; The upper curve of a horse's neck. ; The ridge or top of a wave. ; The summit of a hill or mountain ridge. ; The helm or head, as typical of a high spirit; pride; courage. ; The ornamental finishing which surmounts the ridge of a roof, canopy, etc. ; The top line of a slope or embankment.	a:1rml,143,3;1tvs,123,4;1cby,66,4;15bd,36,5~15bd,36,5;1cby,66,4;1tvs,123,4;1rml,143,3	n:qwt,97,1;2874,66,2;87b,63,3~87b,63,3;2874,66,2;qwt,97,1
