gvi|n|To make the shrill sound characteristic of a cock, either in joy, gayety, or defiance. ; To shout in exultation or defiance; to brag. ; To utter a sound expressive of joy or pleasure. ; A bird, usually black, of the genus Corvus, having a strong conical beak, with projecting bristles. It has a harsh, croaking note. See Caw. ; A bar of iron with a beak, crook, or claw; a bar of iron used as a lever; a crowbar. ; The cry of the cock. See Crow, v. i., 1. ; The mesentery of a beast; -- so called by butchers.	a:a5p,165,5;1uqv,72,1;e3m,41,4~a5p,165,5;e3m,41,4;1uqv,72,1	v:muf,79,3~muf,79,3	n:axw,146,4;1uqv,82,2~axw,146,4;1uqv,82,2
